---
title: Chicken in Honey-butter Sauce
author: Mildred McKinzie
category: Meat, Poultry, Fish
source: Loving Memories of Mildred
---

@frying chicken{1%medium sized}
@whole wheat flour{1%c}
@paprika{2%tsp}
@salt{2%tsp}
@pepper{1/4%tsp}
@butter{1/2%c}
@butter (melted){1/4%c}
@lemon juice{1/2%c}
@honey{1/2%c}

Cut chicken into serving pieces and dip into a mixture of flour, salt, pepper and paprika. Melt @butter{1/2%c} in a baking dish. Add chicken and coat each piece with melted butter. Bake at 400 degrees for 30 minutes, turn and bake about 15 minutes. Serve with Honey-butter Sauce.

**Honey-butter Sauce:**
Combine @butter (melted){1/4%c}, @lemon juice{1/2%c} and @honey{1/2%c} thoroughly and pour over baked chicken.
